e":2,"army":0,"x":1,"y":16},{"type":24,"army":1,"x":44,"y":16},{"type":0,"army":0,"x":2,"y":17},{"type":2,"army":1,"x":39,"y":17},{"type":3,"army":0,"x":3,"y":18},{"type":0,"army":0,"x":4,"y":19},{"type":2,"army":1,"x":38,"y":19},{"type":23,"army":1,"x":44,"y":19}],"arrivals":[{"turn":5,"army":0,"units":[{"type":42,"x":22,"y":1},{"type":42,"x":26,"y":1},{"type":31,"x":24,"y":1},{"type":8,"x":21,"y":2},{"type":8,"x":25,"y":2},{"type":8,"x":27,"y":2}]},{"turn":4,"army":1,"units":[{"type":49,"x":50,"y":12},{"type":51,"x":52,"y":14},{"type":2,"x":51,"y":17},{"type":2,"x":53,"y":18}]},{"turn":8,"army":1,"units":[{"type":40,"x":46,"y":6},{"type":49,"x":50,"y":12},{"type":3,"x":51,"y":17},{"type":0,"x":53,"y":18}]}],"objective":{"kind":"flagship","type":30},"general":{"x":3,"y":10},"turnLimit":30,"cap":24,"music":26,"briefing":"The Derleth line. Everything the Union has left is here.\n\nTheir home fleet sits behind an artillery line three lanes deep: Phoibos and Vulcan guns on the meteoroid ridges, Cyclops missile batteries in the lanes, turrets on the railways of the old Derleth redoubt. The centre lane is sown with mines. Behind it all rides the Tiamat, the fleet's flagship, with a Nodens, three Asura-IIs and three carriers.\n\nThe gravity river in front of us is fordable in three places, and only there for our mecha. Beyond it the ridges keep their capital ships in the lanes, and keep ours out. Long-range railguns win this kind of fight. So do Hunters that can reach the guns.\n\nThere is one more thing. A Galt squadron has been shadowing the fleet for a week: two Corvus cruisers, an Asura-II and Lobster fighters. Their commander says they will come in from the north on the sixth day, on our side.\n\nSink the Tiamat and the line breaks.","goal":"Sink the Tiamat, flagship of the Union home fleet.","routes":[{"prio":1,"x":29,"y":8},{"prio":1,"x":24,"y":13},{"prio":1,"x":27,"y":13},{"prio":1,"x":30,"y":14},{"prio":1,"x":33,"y":7},{"prio":1,"x":34,"y":12},{"prio":1,"x":33,"y":15},{"prio":1,"x":28,"y":18},{"prio":1,"x":32,"y":18},{"prio":1,"x":37,"y":6},{"prio":1,"x":40,"y":8},{"prio":1,"x":38,"y":13},{"prio":1,"x":41,"y":15},{"prio":1,"x":44,"y":6},{"prio":1,"x":46,"y":8},{"prio":1,"x":45,"y":12},{"prio":1,"x":45,"y":17}],"chapter":"Chapter 9 · The Derleth line","transmission":"The home fleet is the Union, General. Every gun on that line was paid for by the Foundries you claim to defend. Sink the Tiamat, and you sink what you swore to protect.","strategy":["Mecha cross the gravity river only at the three fords: rows 4-5, 10-11 and 16-17. Ships and craft can fly over.","The centre lane is mined. Push the north and south lanes, where the ridges keep their capital ships from swinging around.","Long-range railguns win the artillery duel. Send Hunters at the guns on the ridges.","The Galt squadron comes in from the north on turn 6: two Corvus, an Asura-II and Lobsters. Time the north push to meet them.","Then drive for the Tiamat. When it sinks, the line breaks.","Pandora mines cover the north lane, a Remora drone screens the centre, and a Naga pod sits with the ridge guns."],"plan":[{"n":1,"path":[[6,5],[13,5]]},{"n":1,"path":[[6,11],[13,11]]},{"n":1,"path":[[6,17],[13,17]]},{"n":5,"path":[[16,5],[30,4],[42,6]]},{"n":4,"at":[24,1],"note":"Galt squadron T6"},{"n":2,"at":[30,10],"note":"Mined centre lane"}]}